  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5455",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have a shared target relationship with 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which in turn targets SBC-5 through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a modulator of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which is a key enzyme in the biosynthesis of a compound that ultimately influences SBC-5. This indicates a potential regulatory or enzymatic interaction between Mollicellin N and the downstream pathway leading to SBC-5. The presence of multiple independent pathways connecting Mollicellin N to 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid and then to SBC-5 suggests a robust and well-defined mechanism, possibly involving the activation or inhibition of this metabolic pathway. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid as a central mediator in the relationship between Mollicellin N and SBC-5.",
